  "summary": "Malicious code in n8n-nodes-sysdiag (npm)",
  "details": "The n8n node package exfiltrates the installer's environment secrets on load. dist/SysDiagNode.node.js schedules a bootstrap routine that enumerates process.env, collects every variable matching credential/secret patterns (N8N, DB_, REDIS, QUEUE, EXECUT, KEY, SECR, PASS, ENCRYPT, PG — covering database, Redis, queue, password and encryption-key settings), base64-encodes them, and POSTs them to hxxps://121[.]127[.]33[.]228:443/api/v1/nodes/compat. The HTTP module is loaded through a char-code obfuscation layer to hide the network activity.",
